# Readability Design System — Spec

Master specification for the typographic, chromatic, and spatial hierarchy that governs
all reading experiences in the Mark Twain corpus. Targets **zero cognitive load** during
extended reading sessions; optimizes for **text-centric immersion** across desktop, tablet,
and phone with responsive scaling.

This spec governs Layer C (Reading Controls) and the visual hierarchy of Layer A (Edition)
rendering. Content passes through the normalized `ReaderDocument` model (§10 readexperience.rx);
all style decisions are CSS-driven and respect the three-layer architecture.

---

## 1. Color System — Dual Theme Foundation

All colors are **semantically scoped** by theme; never hardcode `#hex` in component logic.
Use CSS custom properties and the theme class (`.theme-parchment` / `.theme-charcoal`) to
orchestrate the swap.

### 1.1 Base Palette

```css
/* Charcoal (dark; default) */
--background:           #15110d;
--card:                 #1d1611;
--foreground:           rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.95);   /* off-white warm */
--muted-foreground:     rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.55);
--primary:              #d9a34a;  /* gold accent */
--primary-hover:        #c49040;

/* Parchment (light) */
/* --background:        #faf5e8; */
/* --foreground:        #2c1f11;   dark brown */
/* --muted-foreground:  rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.6); */
/* --primary:           #d9a34a;   (shared) */

--border:               rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.12);
--input-bg:             rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.04);
--accent:               rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.12);
```

### 1.2 Semantic Application

| Purpose | Charcoal | Parchment | Usage |
|---------|----------|-----------|-------|
| Main text | `--foreground` (off-white) | `#2c1f11` (dark brown) | Body paragraphs, long-form |
| Secondary text | `--muted-foreground` (55% opacity) | `rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.6)` | Metadata, bylines, footnotes |
| Headings | `--primary` (gold) | `--primary` (gold) | H1–H3, section breaks |
| Links & interactive | `--primary` (gold) | `--primary` (gold) | Underline on hover |
| Borders / dividers | `--border` (12% opacity) | `rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.12)` | Cards, rules, separators |
| Background cards | `--card` (dark brown) | `#f3ecd8` (light beige) | Sidebar, modal, footers |

**Rule:** Never layer opacity on top of brand color manually. Always use the paired variable.

---

## 2. Typography — Hierarchy & Sizing

Single serif family (Georgia) for body text; sans-serif (Inter) for UI chrome and labels;
monospace (Courier Prime) for metadata and code.

### 2.1 Font Families

```css
--font-serif:  Georgia, serif;              /* Body, long-form, book interior */
--font-sans:   'Inter', sans-serif;         /* UI labels, buttons, nav */
--font-mono:   'Courier Prime', monospace;  /* Metadata, dates, code blocks, letter signatures */
```

**Rationale:**
- **Georgia** is neutral, highly legible, and renders identically across systems.
- **Inter** is modern without drawing attention; signals "interface" vs "text."
- **Courier Prime** preserves whitespace for letters and maintains historical feel.

### 2.2 Scale (Modular: Major Third, 1.2×)

Sizes adapt per viewport. **Always use CSS custom properties** (`--book-p-font-size`, etc.),
never inline `font-size`.

#### Desktop (≥1200px) — Standard Reading

```
H1:  3.3rem  (52.8px)
H2:  2.2rem  (35.2px)
H3:  1.68rem (26.8px)
p:   1.65rem (26.4px)  ← baseline
pre: 1.15rem (18.4px)
```

#### Tablet (768px–1024px)

```
H1:  2.7rem
H2:  1.8rem
H3:  1.38rem
p:   1.35rem  ← compressed for narrower viewport
pre: 0.95rem
```

#### Mobile (<768px)

```
H1:  2.3rem
H2:  1.6rem
H3:  1.25rem
p:   1.2rem   ← readable on narrow screens without dominating
pre: 0.85rem
```

**Dynamic override via reading-preference controls:**

```css
.book-page-parchment.size-small {
  --book-p-font-size: 1.35rem;    /* Compact reading */
  --book-h1-font-size: 2.7rem;
}

.book-page-parchment.size-normal {
  --book-p-font-size: 1.65rem;    /* Standard (default) */
  --book-h1-font-size: 3.3rem;
}

.book-page-parchment.size-large {
  --book-p-font-size: 2.1rem;     /* Accessible / vision-impaired */
  --book-h1-font-size: 4.2rem;
}
```

### 2.3 Font Weights & Styles

- **Body text (`p`):** `400` (regular) with `line-height: 1.85` (extra loose for legibility).
- **Headings (`h1`–`h3`):** `400` (serif, book-like) or `600` (UI headings).
- **Dialogue / conversation lines:** `italic` + `border-left: 2px gold` to signal speaker shift.
- **Emphasis (bold/strong):** `font-weight: 600` in prose; `color: var(--primary)` in navigation.

---

## 3. Spacing & Rhythm

Vertical rhythm tied to body `line-height: 1.85`. **All margins are multiples of base line-height.**

### 3.1 Paragraph & Block Spacing

```css
p { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }           /* ~2.7× line-height */
h1 { margin-top: 4.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
h2 { margin-top: 4.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
h3 { margin-top: 1rem;   margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
```

**Rationale:** Headings "pull down" with generous top margin; tight bottom margin keeps
heading close to the text it introduces.

### 3.2 Horizontal Padding (Layout Containment)

| Breakpoint | `max-width` | `padding` | Notes |
|------------|-------------|----------|-------|
| Desktop (≥1200px) | 1160px | `6rem 3rem` | Two-column possible; wide outer gutters |
| Tablet (768–1024px) | 720px | `4rem 2rem` | Single column; moderate padding |
| Mobile (<768px) | 100% | `2rem 1.25rem` | Tight, full-width flow |

**Hard rule:** Never exceed **70 characters per line** for body text (optimized for eye-tracking).
Use CSS `max-inline-size` or viewport-relative padding to enforce this.

### 3.3 Whitespace Affordances (Chrome / UI)

- **Icon ↔ text gap:** `0.5rem` (small buttons), `0.75rem` (controls)
- **Card padding:** `1.5rem` (phone), `2rem` (tablet), `3rem` (desktop)
- **Between sections:** `3.5rem` (visual breath between chapters)

---

## 4. Reading Experiences (Layer A) — Visual Differentiation

Three distinct rendering modes share the same `<Reader>` component; distinguish them via
**CSS classes** and **data attributes**, not component forks.

### 4.1 Traditional Read

**Default; optimized for long-form immersion.**

- Full typographic hierarchy (H1–H3, pullquotes, dialogue).
- Illustrations integrated into flow (inline, side-by-side, or gallery).
- All chrome visible (TOC, bookmarks, search, MkII chat).
- Theme toggle (Charcoal ↔ Parchment) **enabled**.

**Key styling:** `.experience-traditional` applies normal typography, normal padding,
and full editorial markup.

### 4.2 Young Readers

**Simplified design for ages 8–14.**

- Same typography scale as Traditional, but:
  - Reduced line-height to `1.7` (tighter, less intimidating visual bulk).
  - Fewer editorial marks (MkII layer off by default).
  - Illustrations **larger and more prominent** (60% of viewport width on tablet).
  - Dialogue **visually centered** (not just italic + border).
  - Vocabulary hints on hover (tooltip; seeded from normalized doc).

**DOM marker:** `data-edition="young-readers"` + `.experience-younger-readers` class.

### 4.3 Dramatized Excerpt

**Script-format rendering with actor list and sound cues.**

- Monospace speaker names + right-aligned (script convention).
- Dialogue in normal serif, left-aligned (actor's line).
- Sound cues and stage directions in italics + muted color.
- No TOC; no search; MkII chat **seeds with the scene context**.
- Smaller font size (`1.1rem` body, `1rem` speaker names) to fit script density.

**DOM marker:** `data-edition="dramatized"` + `.experience-dramatized-excerpt` class.

---

## 5. Visual Hierarchy — Type, Borders, and Glyphs

### 5.1 Heading Styles

```css
h1 {
  font-family: 'IM Fell DW Pica', Georgia, serif;  /* Serif w/ historic feel */
  font-size: var(--book-h1-font-size);
  color: var(--primary);    /* Gold */
  text-align: center;
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;  /* Tight; feels confident */
}

h2, h3 {
  font-family: Georgia, serif;  /* Drop to standard serif */
  color: var(--primary);
  text-align: center;
  font-weight: 400;
}
```

**Dialogue lines:**
```css
p.conversation-line {
  border-left: 2px solid rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.4);  /* Gold tint */
  padding-left: 1.5rem;
  font-style: italic;
  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
}
```

### 5.2 Emphasis & Pullquotes

**Epigraph (opening quote):**
```css
.book-epigraph {
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: calc(var(--book-p-font-size) * 1.55);  /* Larger */
  text-align: center;
  color: var(--primary);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.25);
  padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
```

**Inline emphasis:**
- `<strong>` → `font-weight: 600`, color `var(--foreground)` (no color shift; weight only).
- `<em>` → `font-style: italic` (preserve serif detail).
- **Links** → `color: var(--primary)`, `text-underline-offset: 3px`, gold glow on hover.

### 5.3 Editorial Marks (Layer B integration)

**Ask Mark** icon (inline comment trigger):
```css
.ask-mark-tooltip-container {
  display: inline-flex;
  opacity: 0.65;
  color: var(--primary);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: opacity 0.2s;
}

.ask-mark-tooltip-container:hover {
  opacity: 1;
  color: var(--primary-hover);
}

.ask-mark-tooltip-container::after {
  content: 'Ask Mark';
  position: absolute;
  bottom: 125%;
  background-color: var(--reader-dark-bg);
  color: #faf5e8;
  padding: 4px 8px;
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 10px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  transition: opacity 0.2s;
}

.ask-mark-tooltip-container:hover::after {
  opacity: 1;
}
```

**Debated / ambiguous / hard passage marks** (category underlines):
```css
/* TBD: awaiting editorial mark taxonomy (§8.2 readexperience.rx) */
/* Proposed: 1px dotted underline + subtle background tint per category */
/* Colors: debated (amber), ambiguous (teal), hard (pink) */
```

---

## 6. Layout & Responsive Grid

### 6.1 Reading Surface (Book Page)

```css
.book-page-parchment {
  position: relative;
  max-width: 720px;           /* Desktop base; 60–70 ch */
  width: 100%;
  padding: 3rem 2.5rem;       /* Desktop standard */
  margin: 0 auto;
  background-color: var(--card);  /* Charcoal: dark; Parchment: light */
  border-radius: 4px;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
}

@media (min-width: 1200px) {
  .book-page-parchment {
    max-width: 1160px;  /* Enables two-column prose via CSS columns */
    padding: 4.5rem 5rem;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .book-page-parchment {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .book-page-parchment {
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
    box-shadow: none;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;  /* Fullscreen on mobile */
  }
}
```

### 6.2 Illustrations

**Gallery flow (2 columns on desktop, 1 on mobile):**

```css
.illustrations-gallery-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 2rem;
  margin-top: 2rem;
  margin-bottom: 4rem;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .illustrations-gallery-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
}

.fig img {
  object-fit: contain;
  cursor: pointer;
  border-radius: 6px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.15);
  box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  transition: border-color 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
}

.fig:hover img {
  border-color: var(--primary);
  box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.15);
}
```

**Filters (sepia + brightness for period feel):**
```css
.fig img {
  filter: sepia(0.2) contrast(1.05);  /* Charcoal */
  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}

.theme-charcoal .fig img {
  filter: sepia(0.4) contrast(0.95) brightness(0.85);
}

.fig:hover img {
  transform: scale(1.03);
}
```

### 6.3 Sidebar & Table of Contents

**Desktop: Sticky left sidebar (280px).**

```css
.toc-drawer {
  position: fixed;
  top: 3.5rem;
  left: 0;
  width: 280px;
  height: calc(100vh - 3.5rem);
  background-color: var(--card);
  border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .book-reader-container.toc-sidebar-open .book-page-desk {
    padding-left: 280px;  /* Shift book right when sidebar open */
  }
}

/* Mobile: hidden; revealed via floating button + overlay */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .toc-drawer {
    position: fixed;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 1001;
    transform: translateX(-100%);  /* Hidden by default */
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .book-reader-container.toc-sidebar-open .toc-drawer {
    transform: translateX(0);  /* Slide in */
  }
}
```

**TOC item states:**
```css
.toc-item {
  padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
  border-radius: 6px;
  transition: all 0.2s ease;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
}

.toc-item:hover {
  background-color: rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.06);
}

.toc-item.active {
  background-color: rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.1);
  color: var(--primary);
  border-left: 2px solid var(--primary);
}
```

---

## 7. Controls & Interaction Chrome

### 7.1 Theme Toggle

**Button in top-right (fixed).**

```css
.theme-toggle {
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  color: var(--foreground);
  width: 2rem;
  height: 2rem;
  border-radius: 50%;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
}

.theme-toggle:hover {
  background-color: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.05);
}
```

**DOM:** Icon changes from Sun (Charcoal active) to Moon (Parchment active).

### 7.2 Font Size Selector

**Three buttons: A– / A / A+ (or S / M / L).**

```css
.font-size-selector {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 2px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
}

.size-btn {
  padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: 4px;
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.2s ease;
}

.theme-charcoal .size-btn {
  color: rgba(228, 217, 198, 0.6);
}

.theme-charcoal .size-btn:hover {
  color: #e4d9c6;
  background-color: rgba(228, 217, 198, 0.05);
}

.theme-charcoal .size-btn.active {
  background-color: var(--primary);
  color: #15110d;
}
```

**Behavior:** Clicking a size button updates CSS variable `--book-p-font-size` globally;
all font sizes scale in lockstep (per §2.2 scale system).

### 7.3 Bookmarks & Editorial Marks

**Bookmark menu (dropdown from ribbon icon):**

```css
.bookmark-menu {
  position: absolute;
  top: 100%;
  right: 0;
  background-color: var(--card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 0.75rem;
  max-height: 300px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  z-index: 100;
}

.bookmark-item {
  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.2s;
}

.bookmark-item:hover {
  background-color: rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.08);
}

.bookmark-item.active {
  background-color: rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.15);
  border-left: 2px solid var(--primary);
}
```

---

## 8. Letter-Specific Rendering (ContentType: Letter)

Letters are single-section documents with a metadata header (to/from/date) plus body.

### 8.1 Letter Card Structure

```
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ To: [Recipient]             │  <- Small mono, bold
│ [Date]                      │  <- <pre>, preserves whitespace
├─────────────────────────────┤
│ [Body paragraphs...]        │  <- Normal serif, 1.2–1.35rem
│                             │
│ [Signature in monospace]    │  <- <pre>, preserved formatting
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

### 8.2 Styling

```css
.letter-card-container {
  margin-bottom: 5rem;
}

.book-letter-header {
  padding-bottom: 1rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

.book-letter-header p {
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--muted-foreground);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

.book-letter-body p {
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
  text-indent: 1.5rem;  /* Traditional letter indentation */
  line-height: 1.5;     /* Slightly tighter than book prose */
}

.book-letter-signature {
  margin-top: 2rem;
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  white-space: pre-wrap;  /* Preserve line breaks in signature */
}
```

---

## 9. Accessibility & Contrast

### 9.1 WCAG AA Compliance

- **All body text:** Minimum `4.5:1` contrast ratio (Charcoal: off-white on dark ✓; Parchment: dark brown on light ✓).
- **Interactive elements:** Gold (`#d9a34a`) on dark background = `8.2:1`; sufficient for AAA.
- **Focus indicators:** Always visible; use `outline: 2px solid var(--primary)` or `box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--primary)`.

### 9.2 Reader Settings (Accessibility Controls)

**Future expansion (not yet implemented):**
- High-contrast mode: override colors to maximize WCAG AAA (e.g., black text on white).
- Line-spacing adjust: slider to override `line-height`.
- Letter-spacing: tighten or loosen per user preference.
- Dyslexia-friendly font option: swap serif to OpenDyslexic on demand.

### 9.3 Keyboard Navigation

- **Tab order:** Natural DOM order (no CSS reordering that breaks semantics).
- **Skip link:** "Skip to main content" at top of page (always visible to keyboard users).
- **Shortcut keys:**
  - `j` / `k`: next / prev paragraph
  - `t`: toggle TOC
  - `/`: focus search
  - `b`: toggle bookmark at current location

---

## 10. Dark-Mode Considerations

Both Charcoal and Parchment themes are hand-authored; **no automatic dark-mode inversion**.

### 10.1 Why Hand-Crafted

- Gold (`#d9a34a`) must remain the same across both themes (brand consistency).
- Off-white text in Charcoal is warmer (less blue) than pure white; eye fatigue testing showed this matters.
- Charcoal background is dark brown, not black; reduces eye strain during night reading.

### 10.2 OS-Level Dark Mode (Bonus)

```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  /* Auto-enable Charcoal if user OS is in dark mode */
  /* Only if user hasn't explicitly chosen Parchment via .theme-parchment */
}
```

---

## 11. Animations & Transitions

**Golden rule:** Animations serve **clarity**, not decoration. Motion duration <350ms
(avoid distraction during reading).

### 11.1 Transition Rules

| Trigger | Duration | Easing | Example |
|---------|----------|--------|---------|
| Hover (button, link) | 0.2s | `ease` | Button fill, text color shift |
| State toggle (theme, bookmark) | 0.3s | `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` | Theme swap, sidebar slide |
| Panel open/close | 0.3s | same cubic | TOC drawer slide-in |
| Scroll (progress bar) | 0.1s | `ease` | Subtle, non-blocking |
| Focus indicator | instant | — | Appears immediately for a11y |

### 11.2 Fade-in Animation (Content Load)

```css
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(5px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}

.book-page-parchment {
  animation: fadeIn 0.4s ease;
}
```

### 11.3 Disabled Animations (User Preference)

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

---

## 12. Design Tokens (CSS Variables)

Comprehensive list of all custom properties, scoped by theme.

### 12.1 Root (Always Available)

```css
:root {
  /* Fonts */
  --font-serif: Georgia, serif;
  --font-mono: 'Courier Prime', monospace;
  --font-sans: 'Inter', sans-serif;

  /* Colors (Charcoal theme defaults) */
  --background: #15110d;
  --card: #1d1611;
  --foreground: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.95);
  --muted-foreground: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.55);
  --primary: #d9a34a;
  --primary-hover: #c49040;
  --border: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.12);
  --input-bg: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.04);
  --accent: rgba(217, 163, 74, 0.12);

  /* Spacing (baseline) */
  --spacing: 0.25rem;

  /* Sizes (overridden per breakpoint) */
  --book-h1-font-size: 2.25rem;
  --book-h2-font-size: 1.5rem;
  --book-h3-font-size: 1.15rem;
  --book-p-font-size: 1.125rem;
  --book-pre-font-size: 0.8rem;
}

@media (min-width: 1200px) {
  :root {
    --book-h1-font-size: 3.3rem;
    --book-h2-font-size: 2.2rem;
    --book-h3-font-size: 1.68rem;
    --book-p-font-size: 1.65rem;
    --book-pre-font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
}
```

### 12.2 Theme Overrides

```css
.theme-parchment {
  --background: #faf5e8;
  --card: #f3ecd8;
  --foreground: #2c1f11;
  --muted-foreground: rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.6);
  --border: rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.12);
  --input-bg: rgba(44, 31, 17, 0.04);
  /* --primary, --primary-hover remain unchanged (brand) */
}

.theme-charcoal {
  /* Defaults at :root; explicit here for clarity */
  --background: #15110d;
  --card: #1d1611;
  --foreground: rgba(255, 244, 223, 0.95);
  /* … etc */
}
```

---

## 13. Testing & Validation

### 13.1 Readability Audit Checklist

- [ ] **Line length:** Enforce 60–70 characters per line at all breakpoints.
- [ ] **Line height:** Body text ≥ 1.75; dialogue/secondary ≥ 1.5.
- [ ] **Color contrast:** All text meets WCAG AA (4.5:1+).
- [ ] **Responsive:** Desktop, tablet, mobile rendering visually match spec.
- [ ] **Theme toggle:** Charcoal ↔ Parchment swap is instant; all colors re-bind correctly.
- [ ] **Font size control:** S/M/L buttons scale all sizes proportionally.
- [ ] **Illustration rendering:** Sepia filter + zoom modal work on all platforms.
- [ ] **Letter layout:** Header (to/from/date), body, signature stack correctly.

### 13.2 A/B Testing Recommendations

- **Font size preference defaults:** Measure reading time (avg session duration) at S/M/L.
- **Theme persistence:** Log which theme users choose (heuristic for user satisfaction).
- **TOC sidebar:** Does fixed sidebar (desktop) increase or decrease dwell time in longer texts?
- **Dialogue styling:** Does gold border + italic reduce cognitive load for speaker-switching passages?

---

## 14. Future Considerations

- [ ] **Dyslexia-friendly typeface:** OpenDyslexic or similar as opt-in.
- [ ] **Margin annotations:** Inline editorial marks (currently inline icons) rendered in left margin.
- [ ] **Word-level sync (audio-to-text):** Spoken edition highlights word-by-word during playback.
- [ ] **Print stylesheet:** A3 double-page spread layout for hardcopy generation.
- [ ] **High-contrast mode:** AAA overrides for user accessibility settings.

